Subject: [PATCH 07779/11362] [outer-loop] ARC loop iter6: fix nav engine
 walking through unit-step walls (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5879)

Synthetic robustness probe of the world-model planning path found engine()'s
blocking check used a mid-gap cell (r0+dy//2); for a 1-cell step dy//2==0 sampled
the avatar's own origin, never the destination -> avatar walked through
1-cell-adjacent walls. Masked by tu93 (~6-cell/action jumps). Would make
plan_in_model route through walls on any hidden nav game with unit-step movement.
Fix: swept-footprint check over every entered cell through the destination.
tu93 still solves 3/3 (no regression); 6 regression tests added.

